- The Nyquist rate is twice the highest frequency component in a signal and is given by f_N = 1/T_N.
- The period of the given signal is T = 1/200 = 5 milliseconds.
- The Nyquist rate is f_N = 200/π = 63.66 Hz.
- The Nyquist interval is T_N = 1/f_N = π/63.66 = 0.05 seconds.

**Part (b)**
- The highest frequency component in the square of the signal is twice that of the original signal, so the Nyquist rate is doubled. 
- The Nyquist rate is f_N = 2(200)/π = 127.32 Hz.
- The Nyquist interval is T_N = 1/f_N = π/127.32 = 0.024 seconds.
